{
 "_source": "OSRIC 3.0 Gamemaster Guide, Chapter Twelve — Treasure and Loot. Loot classes §2.12.1 (Hoards 1–9 = §2.12.1.A–I; Individuals 1–5 = §2.12.1.J–N; Caches 1–12 = §2.12.1.O–Z); Unowned Treasure Table 2.12A (§2.12A); Magic-item type Table 2.13.1A (§2.13.1). Gem values Table 2.12.4A and jewellery Table 2.12.5A are held in treasure_valuation.json and rolled from there. Transcribed and verified against docs/OSRIC_Gamemaster_Guide.md.",
 "_note": "Each loot class is a list of 'lines'. A coin/gems/jewellery line with a non-null pct is gated by a d100 roll (present if d100<=pct, per §2.12.1); Individual classes have pct=null (always carried, per creature). 'dice'×'mult' gives the amount (dice module has no × operator, so the multiplier is a separate field). Magic lines list item slots by type; type 'any' is rolled on the §2.13.1A table (respecting any 'exclude'). Coin values in copper: pp=500, gp=100, ep=50, sp=10, cp=1 (Player Guide §1.4.2; 1 ep = ½ gp).",
